{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nA deterministic relocated-store experiment confirmed that `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py::code_root_for` conflates tracker storage with the code repository. `attach_commits` reaches it through `_lib_mutations.py`; with an absolute `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` outside the code checkout, valid code commit SHAs are checked against the tracker parent and rejected. Runtime tracing observed `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse` while the same SHA resolved at the code root.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a real-git held-out regression oracle with a code repository and independently relocated ticket store.\n- Resolve commit validation from `config.repo_root(repo_root)` (explicit root, then `REBAR_ROOT`, then cwd Git top-level), while retaining tracker reads/writes through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`.\n- Remove the obsolete tracker-parent code-root helpers so the invalid derivation cannot remain as unused prior art.\n- Preserve all-or-nothing rejection for unknown SHAs and the default in-repo tracker path.\n- Run RED to GREEN, exact-defect mutation, focused store and attach suites, lint, typecheck, and original CLI replication.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A valid code commit is accepted when the ticket store is outside the code worktree.\n- [x] An unknown SHA remains rejected without recording a partial COMMITS event.\n- [x] Default in-repo tracker behavior remains unchanged.\n- [x] The held-out relocated-store test is observed RED before repair and GREEN after repair.\n- [x] The exact tracker-parent mutation returns the held-out test to RED.\n- [x] `code_root_for` and `unresolvable_shas` have no remaining production definitions or references, checked by repository search.\n- [x] Focused tests pass.\n- [x] `make lint` passes.\n- [x] `make typecheck` passes.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`\n- `grep -R \"code_root_for\\|unresolvable_shas\" src/rebar` must return no matches.\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787045513584145001,"uuid":"adc06ac5-ef2c-4214-9018-4109afb5fd15"}